Let $z = re^{i\theta},$ where $0 \le r \le 1$ and $-\pi/2 \le \theta \le \pi/2.$ Then
\begin{align*}
z^8 - z^6 + z^4 - z^2 + 1 &= r^8 e^{i8\theta} - r^6 e^{i6\theta} + r^4 e^{i4\theta} - r^2 e^{i2\theta} + 1 \\
&= (r^8 - r^6 + r^4 - r^2 + 1) e^{i8\theta} + (-r^6 + r^4 - r^2) e^{i6\theta} + (-r^4 + r^2) e^{i4\theta} + (-r^2) e^{i2\theta}.
\end{align*}The real parts of the terms on the right-hand side cancel, so the imaginary part of the entire expression is equal to the imaginary part of $(r^8 - r^6 + r^4 - r^2 + 1) e^{i8\theta}.$ Since $0 \le r \le 1,$ the coefficient of $e^{i8\theta}$ is nonnegative, so the imaginary part of the entire expression is nonnegative. Equality occurs when $r = 1,$ so the maximum imaginary part of a root is $\sin \theta,$ where $-\pi/2 \le \theta \le \pi/2.$ Setting $\sin \theta = 1,$ we find $\boxed{90^\circ}.$

Final answer: \boxed{90^\circ}

