We have
\begin{align*}
\frac{1}{x^{2^n} - x^{-2^n}} &= \frac{x^{2^n}}{x^{2^{n+1}} - 1} \\
&= \frac{x^{2^n}}{(x^{2^n} - 1)(x^{2^n} + 1)} \\
&= \frac{1}{x^{2^n} - 1} - \frac{1}{x^{2^n} + 1}.
\end{align*}Then
\begin{align*}
\sum_{n = 0}^\infty \frac{1}{x^{2^n} - x^{-2^n}} &= \sum_{n = 0}^\infty \left( \frac{1}{x^{2^n} - 1} - \frac{1}{x^{2^n} + 1} \right) \\
&= \frac{1}{x - 1} - \frac{1}{x^{2^2} - 1} + \frac{1}{x^{2^2} - 1} - \frac{1}{x^{2^3} - 1} + \dots \\
&= \boxed{\frac{1}{x - 1}}.
\end{align*}

Final answer: \boxed{\frac{1}{x - 1}}

